  "body": "## Summary\n- Run `bullet tui` on the outer recorder PTY instead of an inner `pty.fork()` that never received `TIOCSWINSZ` (the published white `operator-tui.gif` cause).\n- Render terminal GIFs with `github-dark` and sample the dark canvas pad (`#171b21`), not `#eceff4`.\n- Add a `CAST_ENTROPY` gate (pre-render in `record-tui.sh` and in `readme-real-check.sh`): refuse printable &lt; 500, zero cursor-position CSI, or zero `38;2`/`48;2` SGR. The current white tape now fails (`printable=104`).\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `bash -n` + `shellcheck -x` on the two shell scripts\n- [x] `readme-real-check.sh --self-test` \u2014 2 accepted, 39 typed refusals including low-entropy white-tape\n- [x] `readme-real-check.sh media/operator-console operator-tui` \u2014 `REAL_MEDIA_CAST_ENTROPY`\n- [x] `record-tui.sh --self-test` \u2014 8 frames, 1920x1080, background `#171b21`, center `#08101f`, amber present\n- [x] `cargo test --locked --test demo_gif_rendering -- --exact terminal_cast_is_preserved_without_inventing_original_rgb_or_font_closure`\n\nDoes not replace `operator-tui.gif` yet (A2, after this lands). HOLD remains. `release_eligible: false`.\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
